  "title": "CoNP-completeness of binary directed chip-firing reachability",
  "description": "<p>Ordinary legal chip-firing reachability is coNP-complete under deterministic polynomial-time many-one reductions for finite loopless strongly connected directed multigraphs, with binary adjacency entries, nonnegative binary initial and target configurations, and varying vertex count. An explicit NONHALTING-to-REACHABLE map uses a finite-state cutoff, exact pre-gate simulation, a gate cleanup budget, and a marker that forces the first gate in every target-reaching word. The complete proof includes loop relays, signed-source threshold normalization, singleton and malformed-input cases, arbitrary target-reaching firing counts, binary output bounds, and the credited reduced-count coNP certificate. It answers the historical general-digraph hardness question in this precise model; no simple-graph, unary, bounded-degree, bounded-chip-count or signed-membership extension is asserted.</p><p>Farrell-Levine supplies source hardness and the total-Laplacian interface; Bj\u00f6rner-Lov\u00e1sz supplies period deletion and reduced counts; Hujter-Kiss-T\u00f3thm\u00e9r\u00e9sz supplies coNP membership and the recurrent-target theorem; T\u00f3thm\u00e9r\u00e9sz supplies the earlier recurrence-to-reachability conversion and hierarchy barrier; Kiss-T\u00f3thm\u00e9r\u00e9sz 2015, Section 4, supplies prior large-reserve finite-horizon simulation. Neither scaling nor reserve simulation in general is claimed as new. Exact-result, gadget and method priority, independent discovery and present-day worldwide openness remain UNKNOWN after the bounded audit. Unavailable and uninspected original sources remain UNKNOWN.</p><p>The upload includes the paper and a portable standard-library verification kit with complete proof source, new exact finite controls and deliberate faults, scoped source metadata, individual custody decisions and deterministic integrity tools. These supplement the written proof; they do not replay the original edition's omitted historical programs or certify a universal theorem by finite tests. AI tools were used extensively in solving, checking, programming, source comparison and writing. This work is unrefereed; internal AI reviews are not external human peer review, journal acceptance or proof-assistant certification.</p>",
